IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Crimes (Biological Weapons) Act 1976 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01649.txt
-- (compilation No. 9, 11 May 2018). The person who holds agents, toxins or
-- equipment, or is charged, asks: "Is what I do unlawful; what is the most I
-- can get; can my material be taken, and for how long; what must happen
-- before I can be committed for trial?"

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `a natural person`
    `a corporation`

-- s 8(1)(a)-(b).
DECLARE `What I hold` IS ONE OF
    `biological agents or toxins of types and quantities with no prophylactic, protective or other peaceful justification`
    `weapons, equipment or means of delivery designed to use them for hostile purposes or armed conflict`
    `agents or toxins justified for peaceful purposes`

-- s 8(1): "develop, produce, stockpile or otherwise acquire or retain".
DECLARE `What I do with it` IS ONE OF
    `develop, produce, stockpile, acquire or retain it`
    `none of these`

-- s 5: where.
DECLARE `Where` IS ONE OF
    `in Australia or an external Territory`
    `outside Australia`

DECLARE `Weapons case` HAS
    `I am`                                                  IS A `Kind of person`
    `I am an Australian citizen`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `where I act`                                           IS A `Where`
    `what I hold`                                           IS A `What I hold`
    `what I do with it`                                     IS A `What I do with it`
    -- s 9(2)
    `it was seized on`                                      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `a prosecution was instituted within the 60 days`       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 10(3)
    `the Attorney-General has consented in writing`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 12(4), (6)
    `I was given the analyst's certificate with reasonable notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the hearing at which I want the analyst called` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Weapons position` HAS
    `I commit an offence`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I may be imprisoned for life`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum fine in penalty units`                         IS A NUMBER
    `it is forfeited to the Commonwealth`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day it may be retained without a prosecution` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `I may be committed for trial`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate can be used against me`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day to notify the prosecutor to call the analyst` IS A DATE

§ `Rules`

-- s 5: the Act reaches acts of Australian citizens outside Australia.
@ref s 5
GIVEN c IS A `Weapons case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act reaches me` c IF
        c's `where I act` EQUALS `in Australia or an external Territory`
    OR  c's `I am an Australian citizen`

-- s 8(1).
@ref s 8(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Weapons case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is unlawful` c IF
        c's `what I do with it` EQUALS `develop, produce, stockpile, acquire or retain it`
    AND NOT (c's `what I hold` EQUALS `agents or toxins justified for peaceful purposes`)

@ref s 8(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Weapons case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I commit an offence` c IF
        `the Act reaches me` c
    AND `it is unlawful` c

-- s 8(2)(a): a corporation, up to 2,000 penalty units; (b): a natural person,
-- imprisonment for a period or for life, or up to 100 penalty units, or both.
@ref s 8(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Weapons case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum units for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`I commit an offence` c) THEN 0
        IF c's `I am` EQUALS `a corporation` THEN 2000
        OTHERWISE 100

-- s 9(1): forfeited where held in contravention of s 8(1), which reaches
-- conduct abroad only of Australian citizens (s 5; changed after the
-- independent pass).
@ref s 9(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Weapons case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is forfeited` c IF `I commit an offence` c

-- s 9(2): retained "until the expiration of a period of 60 days after the
-- seizure", or until a prosecution instituted within it ends.
@ref s 9(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Weapons case`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of retention for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `it was seized on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF c's `a prosecution was instituted within the 60 days`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (d PLUS 60)

-- s 10(3)-(4): a charge, arrest and remand need no consent; committal
-- proceedings do.
@ref s 10(3)-(4)
GIVEN c IS A `Weapons case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I may be committed for trial` c IF
        `I commit an offence` c
    AND c's `the Attorney-General has consented in writing`

-- s 12(4): the certificate needs a copy and reasonable notice; s 12(6)(a): at
-- least 5 days' notice to the prosecutor to call the analyst.
@ref s 12(4)
GIVEN c IS A `Weapons case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is admissible` c IF
    c's `I was given the analyst's certificate with reasonable notice`

@ref s 12(6)(a)
GIVEN c IS A `Weapons case`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give notice for` c MEANS
    c's `the day of the hearing at which I want the analyst called` MINUS 5

@ref ss 5, 8-10, 12
@export default The position of a person who develops, produces, stockpiles, acquires or retains biological agents, toxins or weapons, under the Crimes (Biological Weapons) Act 1976 (Cth): whether it is an offence (s 8: agents or toxins with no peaceful justification, or weapons or means of delivery for them; reaching Australian citizens abroad, s 5); the most that can be imposed (a natural person, imprisonment for a period or for life and 100 penalty units; a corporation, 2,000 penalty units); whether the material is forfeited and the last day it may be held after seizure without a prosecution (60 days, s 9); whether they may be committed for trial (only with the Attorney-General's written consent, s 10); and whether an analyst's certificate can be used and the last day to require the analyst to be called (s 12). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Weapons case`  @desc Who I am and where I act, what I hold and do, any seizure and prosecution, the Attorney-General's consent, and the analyst's certificate
GIVETH A `Weapons position`
`the weapons position for` c MEANS
    `Weapons position` OF `I commit an offence` c,
                          `I commit an offence` c AND c's `I am` EQUALS `a natural person`,
                          `the maximum units for` c,
                          `it is forfeited` c,
                          `the last day of retention for` c,
                          `I may be committed for trial` c,
                          `the certificate is admissible` c,
                          `the last day to give notice for` c
